## Hard rules

1. **Respect the architecture.** The dependency direction described in the
   per-directory `AGENT.md` files is not a suggestion. Do not add an import
   that points the wrong way to "make it work".
2. **TypeScript is strict.** No `any`, no non-null assertions to silence the
   compiler. DTO fields use `!:` because the framework populates them — that
   is the one sanctioned exception.
3. **Adding a module means adding every layer.** A new feature gets its
   full slice; do not put a new entity's logic inside an existing module.
4. **Register new modules** in `src/app.module.ts` or they will not load.
{{#if hasValidation}}
5. **Every request body needs validation.** Never accept an unvalidated DTO.
{{/if}}
6. **Secrets come from `ConfigService`**, never from hardcoded literals or
   direct `process.env` reads outside the config layer.
{{#if useAuth}}
7. **A route is public unless explicitly guarded.** Add
   `@UseGuards(JwtAuthGuard)` deliberately — do not assume auth is enforced
   somewhere else.
{{/if}}
{{#if useTests}}
8. **New use-cases/services get a spec file.** Follow the pattern already in
   each module — mock the repository, do not hit a real database in unit
   tests.
{{/if}}

## When you are unsure

Prefer asking over guessing. Generating a plausible-looking file in the wrong
layer costs more to unpick than a clarifying question costs to answer.
